I think one could tune the amount of randomization of the monster and
the hero movements so that the hero vs. monster is roughly the same as
today, but at least part of the randomness is in the monster movement.

With the current version, you can still get unlucky a few times in a
row - e.g. when Fast:
    if (rn2(3) != 0) moveamt += NORMAL_SPEED / 2;
can fail you three times in a row with probability 1/27, and then
*all* nearby monsters can take advantage of it simultaneously.

There are other interesting effects as well - consider for example
##qqqq#####+.......@...|; if all the rothes move synchronously, they
get to the hero as one pack - randomization could make them separate.

I actually have a patch (just updated for 3.4.2, very little testing as
yet) that randomizes movements of all monsters, while the hero is
deterministic. The patch also changes the whole speed system of the
game and does a few other related things as well, so estimating
gameplay effects of the randomization only is not straightforward.

